WEBVTT

00:00:00.460 --> 00:00:04.860
Aerial perspective can reveal people, homes, routines, property, sensitive locations,

00:00:04.860 --> 00:00:07.000
and security features that were not the mission's purpose.

00:00:07.000 --> 00:00:11.280
Public visibility from above does not remove privacy expectations or the risk created by

00:00:11.280 --> 00:00:12.085
recording,

00:00:12.085 --> 00:00:14.000
aggregation, and distribution.

00:00:14.000 --> 00:00:15.991
Apply data minimization before launch.

00:00:15.991 --> 00:00:20.075
Bound the area, aim sensors carefully, choose no more detail than needed,

00:00:20.075 --> 00:00:22.000
and avoid unnecessary people or private spaces.

00:00:22.000 --> 00:00:24.375
If sensitive content is captured incidentally,

00:00:24.375 --> 00:00:28.000
restrict access and follow approved review and deletion procedures.

00:00:28.000 --> 00:00:29.955
Use requires legitimate authority and proportionality.

00:00:29.955 --> 00:00:35.020
Do not use aerial observation for stalking, harassment, targeting private individuals,

00:00:35.020 --> 00:00:38.385
unlawful surveillance, flight-restriction bypass, interference with aircraft,

00:00:38.385 --> 00:00:40.250
or evasion of accountable oversight.

00:00:40.250 --> 00:00:42.945
Reporting can create harm even when collection was lawful.

00:00:42.945 --> 00:00:48.140
Avoid publishing precise sensitive locations, identifiable people, access vulnerabilities,

00:00:48.140 --> 00:00:49.960
or raw imagery without a defined need.

00:00:49.960 --> 00:00:52.945
Use redaction, aggregation, or controlled distribution when appropriate.

00:00:52.945 --> 00:00:56.980
Access control should separate pilots, analysts, clients, administrators,

00:00:56.980 --> 00:00:59.000
and public recipients according to need.

00:00:59.000 --> 00:01:00.955
Protect accounts, storage, exports, and sharing links.

00:01:00.955 --> 00:01:04.175
Record who approved collection and who received sensitive products.

00:01:04.175 --> 00:01:05.960
Responsible use is explainable.

00:01:05.960 --> 00:01:10.000
The operator should be able to state the purpose, authority, boundaries, evidence,

00:01:10.000 --> 00:01:12.000
uncertainty, retention, and safeguards.

00:01:12.000 --> 00:01:16.970
When safety, legality, privacy, or ethics are unclear, stop and seek qualified guidance.
